From: emilyastranova <emily@astralabs.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: qcom-pmic-typec: count VBUS above vSafe0V as present

TYPEC_VBUS_DETECT in TYPEC_MISC_STATUS only reports VBUS at vSafe5V. When
a USB-PD source accepts a 9 V or 12 V request and steps the supply, the
bit clears during the transition, the port reports "VBUS off", TCPM moves
to SNK_UNATTACHED and the source restarts; the contract never completes
(seen on a OnePlus 7 Pro with a 45 W charger: Accept at +60 ms, VBUS off
at +130 ms, every attach). The stock stack never used this bit for
presence; it used the charger's USBIN plug-in status.

When the detect bit is clear, also look at the Type-C state machine
status, which the driver already polls for vSafe5V/vSafe0V when sourcing:
a supply that is not at vSafe0V is present.
---
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/qcom/qcom_pmic_typec_port.c	2026-10-14 16:52:55.842345722 -0600
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/qcom/qcom_pmic_typec_port.c	2026-10-14 16:52:55.857572096 -0600
@@ -279,15 +279,35 @@
 	unsigned int misc;
 	int ret;
 
+	unsigned int sm = 0;
+	bool vbus;
+
 	ret = regmap_read(pmic_typec_port->regmap,
 			  pmic_typec_port->base + TYPEC_MISC_STATUS_REG,
 			  &misc);
 	if (ret)
 		misc = 0;
 
-	dev_dbg(dev, "get_vbus: 0x%08x detect %d\n", misc, !!(misc & TYPEC_VBUS_DETECT));
+	vbus = !!(misc & TYPEC_VBUS_DETECT);
+
+	/*
+	 * TYPEC_VBUS_DETECT only reports VBUS at vSafe5V. When a USB-PD source
+	 * steps the supply to 9 V or 12 V it clears, TCPM takes that as a
+	 * detach and the contract is torn down during the voltage transition,
+	 * forever. The state machine status also tells whether VBUS sits at
+	 * vSafe0V; anything above that is a present supply.
+	 */
+	if (!vbus) {
+		ret = regmap_read(pmic_typec_port->regmap,
+				  pmic_typec_port->base + TYPEC_SM_STATUS_REG,
+				  &sm);
+		if (!ret && !(sm & TYPEC_SM_VBUS_VSAFE0V))
+			vbus = true;
+	}
+
+	dev_dbg(dev, "get_vbus: misc 0x%08x sm 0x%08x detect %d\n", misc, sm, vbus);
 
-	return !!(misc & TYPEC_VBUS_DETECT);
+	return vbus;
 }
 
 static int qcom_pmic_typec_port_vbus_toggle(struct pmic_typec_port *pmic_typec_port, bool on)
